rategy  we want to understand what our covet  population is  what's our the population of the virus  that we're facing  because that will tell us information  about you know importations  about the viruses diversity about  maybe risks with reinfection as for the  canucks not every player was tested for  the variant but the team just needed one  player to come down with it  to know it was bad we saw how fast  this virus is very contagious the nhl  insist vancouver will finish the season  even though the players are out of  practice robin gill global news  vancouver still ahead a heavy police  presence in northern ireland  along with calls for calm  there's been another night of violence  in northern ireland  despite calls for calm protesters  returned to the streets of belfast  throwing stones and molotov cocktails of  police who used water cannon  to push them back the clashes have  erupted over  long-standing sectarian tensions brought  to life again by  covid by post-brexit trade rules  there are more problems for boeing 737  max  jets boeing has told 16 airlines to  address a  possible electrical fault in some  aircraft before they fly again  the issue was reportedly discovered by  mechanics during production  the 737 max returned to service in  december after being grounded worldwide  in march  2019 changes were made to the automated  flight control system after  it was determined they played a role in  two deadly crashes  he has quite simply been my strength and  stay  all these years next remembering prince  philip who the queen first met  when she was just a girl  [Music]  prince philip was once asked if he was  hoping to reach 100  and he said good god no i can't imagine  anything worse  he said bits of me are falling off  already  he did end up outliving nearly everyone  who knew him and  might be able to explain him those who  are still left describe him  as an unsentimental realist and a  pragmatist he fell in love with his  future wife way back in the 1940s  and that union shaped both the man and  the monarchy  here's jeff semple  on their golden 50th wedding anniversary  back in 1997  the queen gave a rare speech a public  deeply personal tribute to her husband  and i and his whole family and  this and many other countries owe him a  debt  greater than he would ever claim or we  shall ever know  for more than seven decades he stood by  her majesty's side  always a step behind prince philip holds  a unique place in history  no one else served so long as the spouse  of a reigning monarch  they're very much a team and in the  later years they  they really were dependent on each other  much more than we saw  in public behind the scenes of course he  uh he was always head of the family  wore the trousers in private not bad for  a man who wasn't even british  born in greece as a member of the greek  and danish royal families  but after a military coup his family was  banished  in 1939 on the eve of war philip  enlisted in the british royal navy  and during his training was assigned to  watch over his distant cousin  princess elizabeth they exchanged  letters for seven years  and after the war philip asked king  george for permission  to marry his oldest daughter as onto the  famous balcony came  the bride and bridegroom their wedding  in westminster abbey was broadcast to  200 million people around the world  the newlyweds never expected princess  elizabeth was about to become queen  but after her father died suddenly in  1952  she was thrust onto the throne philip  forced to give up his promising naval  career  to assume the full-time job of prince  consort  while elizabeth appeared shy and  reserved phillip was  friendly and even funny i hope you had a  good breakfast this morning because we  may not be through until about tea time  this evening  well i think obviously when he first  started there were quite a few people in  establishment as i say who didn't really  like him  they died away and as time went on of  course he  got older and older and was very much  the establishment himself  and i think he just became more and more  popular with the public mainly for his  outspoken views but those views also got  him into trouble  whole books were written about his  penchant for eyebrow raising remarks  like the time he asked indigenous  australians if they still threw spears  and he was infamously impatient with the  british press  are you well sir do i look ill his  famous stubborn streak was on full  display at the queen's diamond jubilee  pageant in 2012  the 90 year old prince stood in the cold  rain for hours  landing himself in hospital with a  bladder infection  but the duke bounced back visiting  toronto for a quick solo visit in 2013  his final trip to canada we're now going  to see the world's most experienced  place  even into his 90s the royal workhorse  carried out more public engagements than  harry will and kate  combined supporting nearly 800 different  charities  [Music]  in 2017 at the age of 96  prince philip carried out his final  public engagement  before retiring from royal duties but  was still  spotted at family events including the  royal wedding of prince harry and meghan  markle  which phillip attended despite still  recovering from hip surgery  philip is survived by his growing family  children grandchildren and  great-grandchildren  including three generations of future  kings  all heirs to the british throne his  legacy  includes more than 22 000 solo public  engagements and a lifetime of service to  his adopted country  and to the woman who was both his queen  and  his wife he is someone who doesn't  take easily to compliments but he has  quite simply been my strength and stay  all these years and that is global  national for this friday i'm donna  friesen  prince philip made over 70 trips to  canada over his lifetime we leave you  with images  of some of them thanks for watching  you
 

